WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.849
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Cambodia Grade twelve English.

2
00:00:06.149 --> 00:00:09.605
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.905 --> 00:00:16.807
Unit sixteen: Cloze and Error Identification. Today you will find and correct grammar mistakes in a text.

4
00:00:17.107 --> 00:00:19.585
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.533 --> 00:00:23.580
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.417 --> 00:00:25.151
Error.

7
00:00:26.150 --> 00:00:27.720
Error means a mistake.

8
00:00:28.317 --> 00:00:29.318
Find the error.

9
00:00:29.917 --> 00:00:32.232
Your turn. Say: Error.

10
00:00:35.067 --> 00:00:35.882
Error.

11
00:00:36.617 --> 00:00:37.502
Correct.

12
00:00:38.517 --> 00:00:40.214
Correct means to fix.

13
00:00:40.817 --> 00:00:42.050
Correct the sentence.

14
00:00:42.650 --> 00:00:45.326
Your turn. Say: Correct.

15
00:00:48.167 --> 00:00:48.912
Correct.

16
00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:50.663
Agreement.

17
00:00:51.650 --> 00:00:54.033
Agreement means subject and verb matching.

18
00:00:54.617 --> 00:00:56.477
Check subject-verb agreement.

19
00:00:57.083 --> 00:00:59.805
Your turn. Say: Agreement.

20
00:01:02.667 --> 00:01:03.598
Agreement.

21
00:01:04.350 --> 00:01:05.189
Article.

22
00:01:06.183 --> 00:01:08.102
Article means a, an or the.

23
00:01:08.717 --> 00:01:10.171
Use the right article.

24
00:01:10.783 --> 00:01:12.971
Your turn. Say: Article.

25
00:01:15.833 --> 00:01:16.672
Article.

26
00:01:17.417 --> 00:01:18.267
Plural.

27
00:01:19.283 --> 00:01:20.795
Plural means more than one.

28
00:01:21.383 --> 00:01:22.640
Books is plural.

29
00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:25.728
Your turn. Say: Plural.

30
00:01:28.567 --> 00:01:29.440
Plural.

31
00:01:30.183 --> 00:01:31.103
Countable.

32
00:01:32.117 --> 00:01:33.896
Countable means can be counted.

33
00:01:34.483 --> 00:01:35.891
Apple is countable.

34
00:01:36.483 --> 00:01:38.869
Your turn. Say: Countable.

35
00:01:41.733 --> 00:01:42.688
Countable.

36
00:01:43.450 --> 00:01:44.695
Uncountable.

37
00:01:45.683 --> 00:01:48.008
Uncountable means cannot be counted.

38
00:01:48.617 --> 00:01:50.012
Water is uncountable.

39
00:01:50.617 --> 00:01:53.072
Your turn. Say: Uncountable.

40
00:01:55.933 --> 00:01:57.132
Uncountable.

41
00:01:57.883 --> 00:01:59.035
Word order.

42
00:02:00.050 --> 00:02:02.050
Word order means the order of words.

43
00:02:02.650 --> 00:02:03.976
Check the word order.

44
00:02:04.583 --> 00:02:07.317
Your turn. Say: Word order.

45
00:02:10.167 --> 00:02:11.272
Word order.

46
00:02:12.067 --> 00:02:16.089
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:16.950 --> 00:02:19.855
Visal, what errors appear most in exams?

48
00:02:20.950 --> 00:02:34.969
Subject-verb agreement, tense, articles, prepositions, countable and uncountable nouns and word order. Read each sentence slowly and check these points in turn.

49
00:02:36.083 --> 00:02:37.293
Give me an example.

50
00:02:38.383 --> 00:02:48.805
She go to school is wrong because the subject she needs goes. Informations is wrong because information is uncountable. I am agree is wrong because agree is a verb.

51
00:02:49.917 --> 00:02:51.603
How do I check my text?

52
00:02:52.717 --> 00:03:05.472
Read it aloud in your head, underline each verb and check its subject. Then check articles and prepositions. If the sentence sounds odd, look for a small word that is wrong.

53
00:03:06.633 --> 00:03:08.041
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:08.883 --> 00:03:11.707
Grammar focus: common error types.

55
00:03:12.007 --> 00:03:13.113
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:13.817 --> 00:03:15.874
She goes to school every day.

57
00:03:16.783 --> 00:03:18.284
I need some information.

58
00:03:19.233 --> 00:03:26.158
Check agreement, tense, articles, prepositions and countable nouns one by one. Information, advice and furniture are uncountable.

59
00:03:26.917 --> 00:03:30.498
Be careful! Don't say: I need some informations.

60
00:03:32.433 --> 00:03:35.048
Say: I need some information.

61
00:03:35.348 --> 00:03:36.698
Uncountable noun.

62
00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:40.083
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:40.867 --> 00:03:42.181
Find the Mistakes.

64
00:03:42.481 --> 00:03:45.084
Nimol reads a short text full of errors.

65
00:03:46.100 --> 00:03:49.156
He finds that goes should replace go in the first sentence.

66
00:03:50.167 --> 00:03:52.549
He changes informations to information.

67
00:03:53.533 --> 00:03:56.415
He also adds the article the before the library.

68
00:03:57.400 --> 00:04:00.026
At the end he reads the corrected text again.

69
00:04:01.133 --> 00:04:05.205
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:06.050 --> 00:04:07.643
Information is blank.

71
00:04:07.943 --> 00:04:11.713
A, an adjective. B, uncountable. C, plural.

72
00:04:15.267 --> 00:04:17.429
The answer is B: uncountable.

73
00:04:18.583 --> 00:04:19.991
She blank to school.

74
00:04:20.291 --> 00:04:23.700
A, go. B, going. C, goes.

75
00:04:27.267 --> 00:04:28.918
The answer is C: goes.

76
00:04:30.083 --> 00:04:31.433
I am agree is blank.

77
00:04:31.733 --> 00:04:34.713
A, wrong. B, correct. C, formal.

78
00:04:38.267 --> 00:04:40.057
The answer is A: wrong.

79
00:04:41.217 --> 00:04:42.891
What should you check first?

80
00:04:43.191 --> 00:04:46.647
A, title. B, agreement. C, handwriting.

81
00:04:50.200 --> 00:04:52.130
The answer is B: agreement.

82
00:04:53.283 --> 00:04:55.353
At the end Nimol blank the text.

83
00:04:55.653 --> 00:04:59.016
A, burns. B, sells. C, rereads.

84
00:05:02.567 --> 00:05:05.054
The answer is C: rereads.

85
00:05:06.267 --> 00:05:09.639
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:10.483 --> 00:05:12.007
How do you find errors?

87
00:05:20.817 --> 00:05:22.305
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:22.605 --> 00:05:34.026
I read each sentence slowly and underline the verbs. I check agreement, tense, articles and prepositions. Then I read the corrected text again.

89
00:05:34.326 --> 00:05:36.035
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:36.950 --> 00:05:41.251
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and common error types.

91
00:05:41.551 --> 00:05:46.897
Today's value is intellectual honesty. Follow the evidence, even when it is inconvenient.

92
00:05:47.197 --> 00:05:49.872
See you in Unit seventeen. Goodbye!

93
00:05:50.172 --> 00:05:52.442
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

